# =============================================================================
# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# This is not just a build-speed optimisation. Copying the host's bin/ and obj/
# into the image overwrites the container's restore output with project.assets.json
# files that reference Windows NuGet paths, and `dotnet publish --no-restore`
# then fails with NETSDK1064 ("package ... was not found"). Excluding them is
# what makes the build reproducible.
# =============================================================================

# --- .NET build output. See above: these MUST be excluded.
**/bin/
**/obj/
artifacts/
**/TestResults/
**/*.trx
**/coverage/

# --- Node. node_modules is ~400MB and is reinstalled by `npm ci` in the image.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/
**/npm-debug.log*

# --- Secrets. Nothing that could carry a credential enters the build context.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/secrets.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json

# --- Version control and CI.
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
azure-pipelines.yml

# --- Editor and OS.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- Docs and the legacy Web Forms project.
# The Web Forms project targets .NET Framework 4.8 and cannot build in a Linux
# container. It is excluded so it can never be pulled into an image by accident.
docs/
src/legacy/
*.md
!README.md

# --- Docker's own files.
docker-compose*.yml
**/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
